    "answer": {
      "short": "$P(B)\\in[0.3,0.7]$, $P(A\\cap B)\\in[0,0.4]$.\n\nUse $0\\le P(A\\cap B)\\le P(A)$ and rearrange the addition rule.",
      "worked": "Since $A\\cap B\\subseteq A$,\n$$0\\le P(A\\cap B)\\le 0.4.$$\nThe addition rule gives\n$$\\begin{align*}P(B)&=P(A\\cup B)-P(A)+P(A\\cap B)\\\\P(B)&=0.7-0.4+P(A\\cap B)\\\\P(B)&=0.3+P(A\\cap B).\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore,\n$$0.3\\le P(B)\\le 0.7.$$\nThe endpoints are attained when A and B are disjoint and when $A\\subseteq B$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
